---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { contactHref } from '../data/contact';

const pageTitle = 'Privacy policy | Registry Stack';
const pageDescription =
  'What registrystack.org collects, why, and what it does not do: website enquiries, starter requests, analytics, server logs, your rights, and the effective date.';
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <SiteHeader current="privacy" />

  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-hero-title">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h1 id="privacy-hero-title">Privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            This page explains what registrystack.org collects, why, and what it does not do. It
            covers this website only. The hosted lab at lab.registrystack.org and the docs site at
            docs.registrystack.org are separate services with their own policies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-who-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="legal-body">
          <h2 id="privacy-who-title">Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Registry Stack is published by Aubex Consulting LLC, 28 Geary St, Ste 650 #189, San
            Francisco, CA 94108, United States. Aubex is the controller responsible for this
            website. You can reach us through our <a href={contactHref('privacy', 'website privacy question')}>privacy contact form</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-collect-title">What this site collects</h2>
          <p>
            This site is a static set of pages with no accounts. Aggregate analytics, optional
            visit tracking, website enquiries, and starter requests serve different purposes,
            described below.
          </p>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We run a self-hosted analytics tool, Umami, at stats.registrystack.org. It is
            cookie-free. When it is enabled, it records aggregate, de-identified usage data: page
            views, referring sites, and a general browser and device class. It does not build a
            profile of an individual visitor and does not share data with advertising networks. We
            also tag some outbound link clicks, for example to the docs site, the live demo, or
            GitHub, with the link&rsquo;s destination and label, so we can see which resources
            visitors use next. These events are not tied to a name, an email address, or any other
            identifying detail.
          </p>
          <h3>Optional visit tracking</h3>
          <p>
            When optional tracking is enabled, we ask before loading our self-hosted Mautic
            tracker. If you accept tracking, it records the pages you visit on this website,
            referring sites, campaign labels, visit times, and browser and device information.
            We use this history to understand interest in our services. If you then submit a
            non-privacy website enquiry or starter request, we can link your current visits to the
            contact details you provide. A privacy request does not send a browser identifier or
            attach your current visits, even if you accepted tracking. Accepting tracking does
            not sign you up for email marketing.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can reject tracking and still use the website and request a starter. Use
            Tracking preferences in the footer to withdraw your consent or change your choice.
            We also respect browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals. We
            remember your choice in this browser for six months. Withdrawing stops further
            tracking and removes this website&rsquo;s tracking identifiers; it does not itself
            erase information already received. Use our <a href={contactHref('privacy', 'delete tracked information')}>privacy contact form</a> if you want that information deleted.
          </p>
          <p>
            Mautic uses cookies and browser storage to recognize a consenting browser. We remove
            these identifiers when tracking is rejected, or on your next visit after the
            remembered choice expires.
            Page URLs sent to Mautic exclude fragments and query parameters except for a limited
            set of campaign labels. We do not send form contents or email addresses in tracking
            URLs, and we do not share this history with advertising networks.
          </p>
          <h3>Website enquiries</h3>
          <p>
            If you use the contact form, we collect your email address, request type, source page,
            and the message and organization details you choose to provide. We retain this
            information in our self-hosted Mautic system so our team can review the enquiry and
            reply manually by email. Submitting an enquiry does not sign you up for email
            marketing.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the form is unavailable, its recovery link lets you email us. If you use it or
            reply to us by email, we receive your email address and the content of your message.
            We use that information to handle the request and keep the exchange as ordinary
            business correspondence.
          </p>
          <h3>Starter requests</h3>
          <p>
            If you use a starter request form, we collect your email
            address and any organization, role, or request details you choose to provide. We also
            record the starter requested, the time of the request, and the source page. We retain
            this information in our self-hosted Mautic system so our team can review the request
            and reply manually.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our servers receive your network address to process requests and use temporary
            rate-limit counters to limit abuse. Mautic is configured to anonymize IP addresses.
            If you have not accepted tracking, we do not send a browser identifier with your
            enquiry or request or attach your current visits to it. Privacy requests follow this
            rule even if tracking was accepted. If you accept tracking and it is available, a
            non-privacy form sends the browser identifier so Mautic can attach your current visits
            to the enquiry or request. Previously stored correspondence or visit history is not
            erased automatically. Submitting an address does not verify that you own it or grant
            access to any account. There is no automatic marketing signup.
          </p>
          <h3>Server logs</h3>
          <p>
            This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub, as the hosting provider, keeps its own
            server logs, for example request IP addresses, to operate the service. We do not
            configure or query those logs beyond what GitHub provides. GitHub&rsquo;s own privacy
            statement covers that data.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our form and tracking servers also receive network addresses and browser headers
            to respond to requests and operate the service. Requests to the optional Mautic
            tracker start only after you accept tracking.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-not-title">What this site does not do</h2>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>It does not require tracking consent to submit a starter request.</li>
            <li>It does not run advertising and does not share data with ad networks.</li>
            <li>It does not sell personal data.</li>
            <li>It does not load the Mautic visit tracker before you accept tracking.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="privacy-basis-title">Legal bases for visitors in the EEA and UK</h2>
          <p>
            Where the GDPR or the UK GDPR applies, we rely on legitimate interest to run
            aggregate, cookie-free analytics that help us understand which pages are useful.
            Optional Mautic visit tracking relies on your consent, which you can withdraw at any time. If
            you submit a website enquiry or starter request, that exchange proceeds on the basis
            that you chose to contact us and provided your information for that purpose.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-retention-title">Retention</h2>
          <p>
            Analytics events are aggregate and are not tied to an identified person. We keep them
            only as long as they are useful for understanding site usage. Website enquiries,
            starter requests, and related email correspondence are kept as ordinary business
            records for as long as they stay relevant. Optional visit histories are held in our
            self-hosted Mautic system and
            are separate from the six-month browser preference. Withdrawing consent does not
            automatically delete those records; you can request their deletion through the privacy
            contact form.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-rights-title">Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us to access, correct, or delete personal data you have given us, for
            example a starter request or website enquiry, through our <a href={contactHref('privacy', 'access, correction, or deletion request')}>privacy contact form</a>.
            We will respond. Aggregate analytics data is not tied to an identified person, so there
            is generally nothing to look up or erase per visitor. If you believe otherwise in your
            case, tell us and we will look into it.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-third-party-title">Third-party services linked from this site</h2>
          <p>
            This site links to GitHub for source code and releases, to docs.registrystack.org for
            documentation, and to lab.registrystack.org, a hosted demo that runs on synthetic data
            only. Each of those is a separate service with its own privacy practices. This policy
            covers registrystack.org only.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-changes-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this page as the site changes. The effective date below tells you when
            it last changed.
          </p>

          <p class="legal-effective">Effective date: October 24, 2026.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-body {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    margin-top: 44px;
  }

  .legal-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .legal-body p {
    color: var(--registry-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .legal-body .check-list {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .legal-effective {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule);
    color: var(--registry-muted);
    margin-top: 44px;
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
</style>
